    "appVersion": "0.1.0-alpha",
    "author": "Optibench examples",
    "created": "2026-11-19T00:00:00.000Z",
    "description": "White light from a 5778 K (sunlight-like) source passes through an equilateral F2 flint prism set near minimum deviation (~48.5 deg at 555 nm). Because the index of F2 rises towards the blue, violet leaves about 4 deg steeper than red. A silver fold mirror turns the fan back to horizontal, a 50/50 plate splitter sends half to a spectrometer and half to a screen where the rainbow lands (red at one end, violet at the other).",
    "dimension": "2d",
    "modified": "2026-11-19T00:00:00.000Z",
    "title": "Prism Rainbow"
  },
